"""Approximate a boundary-sensitive component with text-level rules.

Document beginnings have a positive offset, also kept during an initial run of
identical tokens. Most later tokens are near zero. A few function words after
separator dashes and bars receive negative responses. After spaced hyphens,
words uncommon in English receive stronger negatives near a document's start.
There are larger responses to subtracting a parenthesized negative,
a warning's '-- Docs' footer, and parenthesized @handles in tweet attributions.
